 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 528609,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>The file <a href=\"https://openstax.org/r/Chapter8_Data-Sets\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">“InState”</a> contains in-state tuition costs (in dollars) for every institution of higher learning in the United States for which data is available (data from data.ed.gov). Create a histogram in Google Sheets of in-state tuition costs. Choose a bin size that you think works well. Are the data uniformly distributed, symmetric, left-skewed, or right-skewed?</p>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Watch the video in the lesson.</p>\n<p>Open a copy of the file from the lesson in Google Sheets.</p>\n<p>See the InState tuition costs on the second tab.</p>\n<p>Highlight ONLY column B and C (not all three columns).</p>\n<p>In the top menu, choose “Insert” and then choose “Chart.”</p>\n<p>It likely will suggest “Histogram” in “Chart type.” If not, change it to “Histogram.”</p>\n<p>Select “Customize,” then select the “Histogram” options.</p>\n<p>Bucket size: You can change “Auto” to anything you like. You will have to select a preset number first, but then you can type in a number such as 2,500.</p>\n<p>To add axis labels, select “Chart and axis titles.”</p>\n<p>In the drop down, select “Horizontal axis title” and enter “Tuition.”</p>\n<p>In the drop down, select “Vertical axis title” and enter “Frequency,”</p>\n<p>Once you have created your histogram, you can see that the data are strongly right skewed.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<p>Answers may vary based on bin choices. Here’s the result for bins of width 2,500:</p>\n<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBaHNHIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--509fee649dfdc01b46588be77199e8969f056fd7/CS_Figure_08_02_021.jpg\" alt=\"A histogram of in-state tuition costs at US institutions. The horizontal axis representing tuition ranges from 2500 to 75000, in increments of 2500. The vertical axis representing frequency ranges from 0 to 800, in increments of 200. The histogram infers the following data: 2500, 230. 5000, 680. 7500, 480. 10000, 390.  12500, 300. 15000, 390. 17500, 270. 20000, 175. 22500, 150. 25000, 100. 27500, 120. 30000, 150. 32500, 160. 35000, 120. 37500, 100. 40000, 90. 42500, 80. 45000, 70. 47500, 60. 50000, 50. 52500, 50. 55000, 70. 57500, 50. 60000, 10. 75000, 10. Note: all values are approximate.\">\n<p>The data are strongly right-skewed.</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
